    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1="1" ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Golden Hope, Hatter&apos;s Castle:
Hatter&apos;s Castle was the first colonial style bungalow built on Carey Island, Selangor in 1923 by a Danish engineer, Gjorup. The name &apos;&apos;Hatter&apos;s Castle&apos;&apos; was inspired by A.J. Cronin&apos;s novel by that name. The founder of Carey Island, Edward Valentine Carey resided in this bungalow during the initial years of the island&apos;s development. For the last 20 years, Hatter&apos;s Castle has been used as VVIP  guesthouse for senior executives of the Golden Hope Group and guests of the company.</marc:subfield>
